{title: Nearer, My God, to Thee}
{artist: Sarah F. Adams}
{key: G}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 6/4}
{meta: tune BETHANY - Lowell Mason (1856)}
{meta: public_domain Text 1841, tune 1856: both published before 1931 (US public domain); all authors, translators and composers died over 70 years ago. Chords and section layout: original simple arrangement by Tabernacle Tools. Original verses only, no modern additions.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Nearer, my [C]God, to [G]Thee, nearer to [D]Thee!
[G]E'en though it [C]be a [G]cross that [D]raiseth [G]me;
Still all my [D]song shall be, [G]nearer, my [D]God, to Thee,
[G]Nearer, my [C]God, to [G]Thee, [D]nearer to [G]Thee!
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Though like the [C]wanderer, [G]the sun gone [D]down,
[G]Darkness be [C]over [G]me, my [D]rest a [G]stone;
Yet in my [D]dreams I'd be [G]nearer, my [D]God, to Thee,
[G]Nearer, my [C]God, to [G]Thee, [D]nearer to [G]Thee!
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]There let the [C]way ap[G]pear, steps unto [D]heaven;
[G]All that Thou [C]sendest [G]me, in [D]mercy [G]given;
Angels to [D]beckon me [G]nearer, my [D]God, to Thee,
[G]Nearer, my [C]God, to [G]Thee, [D]nearer to [G]Thee!
{end_of_verse}
